egl, zink: a macOS EGL platform, zink through kopper with VK_EXT_metal_surface

OpenGL on macOS without Apple's OpenGL: EGL on zink, on a Vulkan driver that
has VK_EXT_metal_surface (ANV over B580.kext here, or MoltenVK/KosmicKrisp).

egl: a native platform "macos" (_EGL_PLATFORM_MACOS, the default display with
-Dplatforms=macos). EGLNativeWindowType is a CALayer * (a CAMetalLayer or an
NSView's backing layer), as with ANGLE's Metal back end, so GLFW's EGL context
API on Cocoa works unchanged. There is no DRM device: the platform loads zink,
which picks its Vulkan device itself. Window surfaces are kopper drawables
(VkMetalSurfaceCreateInfoEXT on the layer), sized by the layer's bounds times
its contentsScale; pbuffers as on the surfaceless platform; swap intervals 0
and 1. Windows are opaque, as with NSOpenGL, unless the application made its
NSWindow non-opaque (GLFW_TRANSPARENT_FRAMEBUFFER): the layer is marked opaque
with a black background and the swapchain's presenting sublayer's contents
opaque (contentsOpaque), so an application that leaves alpha 0 in the window
framebuffer (Minecraft blits with alpha writes masked) is not see-through.
MESA_MACOS_OPAQUE=0 leaves the layer alone.

egl/surfaceless: without a DRM device, MESA_LOADER_DRIVER_OVERRIDE=zink (and
the zink fallback of eglInitialize) uses zink's own device choice, as
LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE does.

zink: kopper presents to VK_EXT_metal_surface surfaces (KOPPER_METAL; the
instance enables the extension when the loader has it).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

